Flags are hexadecimal: 0x10 INEXACT, 0x04 OVERFLOW. The exact binary64
representation of the input float is 47efffffe0000000. Upward's polynomial
result exceeds it by 0x45 binary64 ULPs. Narrowing this approximation to float
under upward rounding produces infinity and flags 0x14. Narrowing the exact
input representation produces the original finite float and no flags.
The explicit early-overflow comparison is FALSE in all four modes: this failure
is not that branch firing. log2 has already raised INEXACT, so adding a late
identity-value correction alone would not repair the library's flag contract.

The source has no y==1 bypass before its log/exp approximation. The reduction,
three independent compiler paths and both archives localize the recorded test
failure to that pinned numerical algorithm; no EvoCC instruction discrepancy
was found. Repairing the library or updating its pin would be a distinct
configuration, not unchanged-benchmark PASS. Other powf inputs are not closed.

An intermediate inline observer let GCC O2 reuse exp2's earlier value across a
